      "markdown": "## Gender\n\nIt has long been acknowledged that there may be differences in language usage between men and women: quite extreme in languages other than English\n\n• Lakoff (1975) identified extensive differences not just in grammar and lexis, but in aspects of style, register, and (especially in dialogues) dynamic roles\n\n• Studies have adapted to the broader social agenda: early theories relating to power relationships between sexes (Lakoff) now giving way to view that there is a cultural difference (Tannen)\n\n• We'll look at this issue in more detail later",
